WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.270
Open a French novel and
the verbs look strange:

2
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.130
«il fut», «ils vinrent».

3
00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.820
Even «il vit» is a trap:

4
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.450
one spelling, two different verbs.

5
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.610
Now stretch that across a whole book,

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.500
in your second language.

7
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.910
And the extract you talk about
could come from any page.

8
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.250
So how do you read it well
enough to talk about any page,

9
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.350
in French? In this mission,

10
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:27.240
you'll crack those strange
story verbs with a pattern grid.

11
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.600
Then you'll link a Maupassant story,

12
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.030
«La Parure», to big themes on a theme web.

13
00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.540
Your mission: find out how to read a whole

14
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.190
novel so that no page catches you out.
